From 4a4182e644673ef79e26746b9efe7cb921c7a157 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: applejack9050 <applejack9050@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 18 Aug 2026 22:49:37 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 2/4] feature: fuse SIFT match row reduction, drop the full dot
 matrix

MultiplyDescriptor_Kernel wrote a complete num1 x num2 matrix of
descriptor inner products to global memory, and RowMatch_Kernel read all
of it back just to take a best/second-best per row. That round trip
dominated the matcher: after the DP4A change ncu showed the multiply
kernel memory-bound at 95.2% with DRAM at 55.7%.

The column direction already avoided this -- each block reduced its 8
rows into one triple per column and ColMatch_Kernel merged the partials.
Do the same in the row direction: reduce each block's 128 columns to one
(best, index, second_best) triple per row with warp shuffles, and let
RowMatch_Kernel merge the gridDim.x partials. The dot matrix is never
materialized.

_texDot is replaced by _texRRT, which is allocated as max_sift x
ceil(max_sift/128) triples rather than max_sift squared ints. That
buffer scaled quadratically with the feature count and was by far the
largest allocation in the matcher.

Exactness: seeding each lane from the identity (0, -1, 0) and keeping
the left operand on ties in MergeBest reproduces the original scan,
which also started at zero with index -1 and advanced only on a strict
increase. So a zero dot product still never matches, the lowest column
index still wins ties, and the guided kernel's rejected pairs are still
clamped with max(.., 0). The reduction is inlined rather than factored
into a helper taking `results` by pointer, because passing a local array
to a callee is the pattern NVCC miscompiles on Blackwell (#3514).

RTX 5090 (sm_120), 40 images of south-building, 780 pairs:
  RowMatch_Kernel            315us -> 25us   (-92%)
  MultiplyDescriptor_Kernel  667us -> 629us
  matching GPU total        1015ms -> 768ms
  matcher peak GPU memory   1762MiB -> 952MiB (-46%)
Against the unmodified matcher the totals are 1166ms -> 768ms (-34%).

Match counts are identical to the original, 201757 over 780 pairs.
End-to-end on 20 images both register 20/20 at 0.552 vs 0.553 px mean
reprojection error; that spread and the two_view_geometries counts stay
inside the run-to-run RANSAC noise of the unmodified binary.

